cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Dose Banding Algorithm"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hopkins
    given-names: Sean P.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO: add before minting the DOI
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lumina-Bridging-Inc/dose-banding-algorithm"
abstract: >-
  Generates standardised chemotherapy dose bands with a guaranteed tolerance
  bound, in a format that imports directly into a CPOE standardised dose range
  table. For every configuration it accepts, the generated table is verified to
  satisfy three properties before being returned: every band dose is a whole
  number of syringe graduations, every prescribed dose in range receives a band
  dose within the stated tolerance judged at the published boundaries, and the
  bands tile the range with no gap and no overlap. Where the guarantee cannot be
  met the algorithm refuses rather than emitting a non-compliant table.
keywords:
  - dose banding
  - chemotherapy
  - oncology pharmacy
  - CPOE
  - medication safety
license: MIT
version: "1.0"
